[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Direct Rust circuit admission and wire preservation

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: CIRCUIT-RUST-ADMISSION-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Validate numerical inputs at the public Rust boundary
STATEMENT: >>>
Circuit validation shall independently reject nonfinite or nonpositive passive
values and nonfinite independent source values. Finite zero and negative source
values shall remain valid. These checks shall apply to direct Rust objects,
without depending on an earlier JSON decoder rejecting nonfinite numbers.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: tests/circuit_admission.rs passive_values_are_independently_positive_and_finite
and source_values_require_finiteness_but_allow_zero_and_negative_values.
Positive-scale property:64Proptest cases, seed2026111915. No convergence claim.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: CIRCUIT-MODEL-PORTS-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Independently admit model ports and control parameters
STATEMENT: >>>
Circuit validation shall independently reject out-of-range gate/body or
back-gate ports for the named MOS1, bulk BSIM3 and FD SOI reference elements.
Junction Early-effect controls shall independently validate their node indices
and positive finite voltage scale with finite reciprocal. Both junction element
variants and MOS1 channels shall validate their model parameters before use.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: each_early_control_operand_is_validated_independently,
model_gate_and_body_ports_are_checked_without_loading_a_provider,
both_junction_element_variants_validate_the_model. Valid controls also execute.
This admission-only scope does not qualify native providers, constitutive laws,
charge behavior or the native_mos adapter accessor.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: CIRCUIT-OFFSET-WIRE-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Preserve nonunit current-control offsets across serialization
STATEMENT: >>>
Serialization shall retain a nonunit voltage-scaled CCCS factor offset.
An omitted legacy offset shall deserialize to exactly one; omitting the unit
offset on output shall preserve its roundtrip meaning.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: nonunit_factor_offsets_survive_the_wire_roundtrip tests negative,
zero, fractional, unit and positive nonunit values. This tests Element wire
semantics alone, not whether a referenced controlling branch exists.
<<<
